{# The library's rail - **the wiki's rail, derived rather than reinvented**
   (design/validated/file-library.md). Same gestures, same states, class shapes mirroring
   `cm-wiki__rail`, because there must not be two implementations of one tree in this application.

   Four deliberate differences, each with a reason:

     - the quota bar sits at the very top, above the title: it answers the question actually being
       asked - « est-ce que je peux encore déposer ? » - at the moment it is asked;
     - the rail holds **folders only**. Files are the table's business; a rail listing both would be
       the same list twice;
     - **no counters** here. The rail navigates and receives a drop, it does not measure - the count
       lives in the table, next to something you can act on;
     - the foot is **pinned to the bottom of the block** (`margin-top: auto`), and carries a button
       on the left and a link on the right: creating a folder is daily housekeeping, the corbeille is
       a rarely-opened back door, and the difference should be visible without being read. #}
<aside class="cm-flib__rail" data-controller="file-library-tree"
       data-file-library-tree-move-url-template-value="{{ path('app_file_library_node_move', {nodeId: '__NODE_ID__'}) }}"
       data-file-library-tree-token-value="{{ csrf_token('file_library_node') }}"
       data-file-library-tree-refused-message-value="{{ 'fileLibraryMoveRefusedMessage'|trans }}"
       {# dragstart/dragend are listened for on the whole screen by the controller itself: what is
          dragged is a row of the table, which is outside this element (see the controller). #}
       data-action="dragover->file-library-tree#dragOver dragleave->file-library-tree#dragLeave drop->file-library-tree#drop">

    {# Two lines, a 4px track, no heading: an ambient indicator, not a figure somebody comes to
       consult. It exists in exactly two places on the platform - here and on the admin's user
       sheet - and deliberately neither in the action bar nor in the upload component. #}
    <div class="cm-flib__quota cm-flib__quota--{{ quota.level }}">
        <div class="cm-flib__quota-line">
            <span>{{ quota.usedLabel }} / {{ quota.limitLabel }}</span>
            <span class="cm-flib__quota-percent">{{ quota.percent }} %</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cm-flib__quota-track">
            {# Capped at 100 for the *drawing* only: over quota the bar is full and red, and the
               figure above it still reads 118 %, which is the number to act on. #}
            <div class="cm-flib__quota-fill" style="width: {{ min(quota.percent, 100) }}%"></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cm-flib__rail-head">
        <span class="cm-flib__rail-title">{{ 'fileLibraryRailTitleLabel'|trans }}</span>
    </div>

    {% if rail is empty %}
        <p class="cm-flib__rail-empty">{{ 'fileLibraryRailEmptyText'|trans }}</p>
    {% else %}
        <ul class="cm-flib__tree" data-file-library-tree-target="root">
            {% for row in rail %}
                {% include 'file_library/_rail_node.html.twig' with {row: row, currentFolder: currentFolder|default(null)} only %}
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="cm-flib__rail-foot">
        <button type="button" class="cm-btn cm-btn--sm cm-btn--outline"
                data-action="file-library#promptFolder"
                data-parent-id="{{ currentFolder ? currentFolder.id : '' }}">{{ 'fileLibraryNewFolderAction'|trans }}</button>
        <a href="{{ path('app_file_library_trash') }}" class="cm-flib__rail-link cm-flib__rail-link--end">{{ 'fileLibraryTrashNavLabel'|trans }}</a>
    </div>
</aside>
